Overloading

Methods name same, parameters different, return type can also be different

************************************************************
1) Method overloading supports polymorphism
2)
If no matching method is found. Java can automatically convert an integer into a double

class OverloadDemo {
void test() {
System.out.println("No parameters");
}
void test(double a) {
System.out.println("Inside test(double) a: " + a);
}
}
class Overload {
public static void main(String args[]) {
OverloadDemo ob = new OverloadDemo();
int i = 88;
ob.test();
ob.test(10, 20);
ob.test(i); // this will invoke test(double)
}

